/-!
# Borel determinacy and analytic determinacy (wanted)

Two determinacy theorems beyond the Gale–Stewart theorem
(`MathlibExt.SetTheory.Determinacy.determined_of_isClosed`):

* Martin's theorem (1975), recorded here with a deferred proof: every Borel game on any non-empty
  set of moves is determined. It is provable in ZFC but needs the axiom of replacement: Friedman
  (1971) showed it is not provable in Zermelo set theory with choice (Woodin, *The continuum
  hypothesis, Part I*, Notices AMS 48 (2001)).
* Martin's theorem (1970): if a measurable cardinal exists, every analytic (`Σ¹₁`) subset of
  Baire space is determined. ZFC alone does not prove this (Moschovakis, *Descriptive Set
  Theory*, 2nd ed., AMS 2009, Exercise 6A.12). It is proved in
  `MathlibExt.SetTheory.Determinacy.AnalyticDeterminacy`, which this module imports.
-/

@[expose] public section

open MeasureTheory

namespace MathlibExt.SetTheory.DeterminacyWanted

open MathlibExt.SetTheory.Determinacy

universe u

/-- **Martin's Borel determinacy theorem.** For every non-empty set of moves `A`, every Borel
payoff set `S ⊆ A^ℕ` (for the product of the discrete topologies) is determined
(D. A. Martin, *Borel determinacy*, Ann. of Math. 102 (1975) 363–371; Moschovakis,
*Descriptive Set Theory*, 2nd ed., AMS 2009, Theorem 6F.1, which also allows games with rules).
The Borel sets here are those of the σ-algebra generated by the open sets, as in Moschovakis §6A;
`A` may be uncountable. -/
theorem_wanted determined_of_measurableSet_borel {A : Type*} [Nonempty A] [TopologicalSpace A]
    [DiscreteTopology A] {S : Set (ℕ → A)} (hS : MeasurableSet[borel (ℕ → A)] S) :
    Determined S

end MathlibExt.SetTheory.DeterminacyWanted
